{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : G\\to H$", "MATH_0002": "$p$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-group-groupoid}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-group-homomorphism-functor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:907dd579c3eb4d4adf277167e56cda44dad8836e0a96f81e61866246f022dcd0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:47dacdd04e47c4c6716828c818b258bb985a67e04319c3ede73764e910dae2b4", "source_text": "A homomorphism <MATH_0001> of groups gives rise to a functor\nbetween the associated groupoids in Example <REF_0001>. It is\nfaithful (resp.<SPACE_0001>fully faithful) if and only if <MATH_0002> is injective (resp.<SPACE_0002>an\nisomorphism).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4bd00b6f50f219d121b415440cd52b6fa9491175b41728e6e4c0d2a3878edab8", "unit_id": "tag:001F:statement"}
